{
  "title": "E2E Tests for Repo CLI",
  "iterations": [
    {
      "prompt": "The repo cli should be tested e2e for all commands with all different syntaxes (positional, flags, named values). Never interact with github on tests and cleanup afterwards. Dont create any new test files but extend the existing test file. A single tests should always cover one unit and do multiple tests for that unit. Make sure all tests pass. Change/refactor/extend whatever is necessary to get it working. Even if it seems unrelated to you. The goal is clear. Dont ask in between, no confirmations, no matter the issue. Figure it out. Be sure that it works everywhere before stopping. Make sure to open and close a ticket. Dont forget to track everything (plan, todos, changes, summary, etc) in .semio-repo/tickets/YYYY/MM/DD/TICKETSLUG/ticket.md Dont keep any legacy api or backwards compatiblity.",
